From fe739c571db05c0741aaf463c022656f2921587e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergei Rudenkov <sergeirudenkov@google.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:59:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/32] [DevTools] Attribute "Open in new tab" navigations to
 the inspected page

DevToolsWindow::OpenInNewTab() opened URLs with a browser-initiated
navigation that had no initiator origin. Such navigations are
indistinguishable from URLs typed into the omnibox: the request carries
SameSite=Strict cookies and `Sec-Fetch-Site: none`. Since the URL usually comes from content controlled by the inspected page (console output, requests in the Network panel, ...), this allowed a page to have the user issue a GET that bypasses the CSRF defenses of a cross-site destination.

Set initiator_origin, initiator_frame_token, initiator_process_id and
source_site_instance from the inspected page's primary main frame, like
the context menu does for "Open link in new tab". Cross-site destinations now see `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site` and no SameSite=Strict cookies; same-site destinations are unaffected. No Referer is sent, as before.

Bug: 554558674
Bug: 576204004
